  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe serves 4 as a side dish and takes around 35 minutes. Japanese potato salad is softer and creamier than its European cousins. The potatoes are mashed just enough to break them up rather than being left in chunks, and the dressing is made with"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Japanese mayonnaise"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "and a splash of"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "rice vinegar"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Thin slices of cucumber, carrot, and sometimes ham are folded through. Serve cold or at room temperature alongside a main dish."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Dress the hot potatoes with the rice vinegar as soon as they come out of the water. The warm potato absorbs the vinegar and develops a subtle tang. Leave to cool completely before adding the mayonnaise. Adding mayo to hot potato melts it into a greasy pool and the salad will not hold its texture."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "potatoes-floury",
              "amount": 600,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "peeled and cut into 3cm chunks",
